          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has focal epilepsy with onset at 8 years of age. Seizures are focal to bilateral tonic-clonic and currently occur approximately once per week. The epilepsy is drug-responsive.\n\nCurrent Antiseizure Medications:\n- Lacosamide\n- Valproate\n\nSeizure Burden:\nApproximately 1 focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizure per week.\n\nAssessment:\nFocal epilepsy of structural etiology, with focal to bilateral tonic-clonic seizures. MRI finding is encephalomalacia. Epilepsy is drug-responsive.\n\nPlan:\nContinue the current antiseizure medication regimen of lacosamide and valproate. Continue monitoring seizure frequency.\n\nSincerely,\nEpilepsy Clinic",
